  "body": "It's not strictly a feature request or a bug report, and I couldn't get any luck in the Matrix room, so I'm asking here. Releasing the files as a TAR seems very unnecessary, as it increases the amount of data that needs to be downloaded almost 50 fold. What's even more confusing is why the archive is then compressed, which saves nearly no storage but adds decompression time to extracting the required DEB. What's the reasoning behind this?",
